# Performance

- Measure before optimizing when a bottleneck is not obvious.
- Prefer algorithmic and I/O improvements over micro-optimizations.
- Watch database query counts, network round trips, serialization, memory growth, bundle size, and unnecessary rendering.
- Preserve correctness, observability, and maintainability while optimizing.
- For performance-sensitive changes, state the expected bottleneck and how it was verified.
